# Build context for chatbot-backend and vector-context-manager is the REPO ROOT,
# not the service directory, because both compile ../shared/src into their own
# dist (tsconfig rootDir is "../"). Docker reads the .dockerignore next to the
# context root, so this file - not a per-service one - is what applies to them.
#
# cms/ has its own context (Root Directory = cms) and its own .dockerignore;
# nothing here affects it.

**/node_modules

# Must be excluded. vector-context-manager's tsconfig "include" is ["./"], so a
# stale dist/**/*.d.ts copied into the image makes tsc fail with duplicate
# declarations - this is the same hazard its `rm -rf ./dist` build step guards
# against locally.
**/dist

# Secrets are supplied by Railway's environment, never baked into a layer.
**/.env
**/.env.*

**/.git

# Local Chroma server data dir (created by `npm run chroma-server`). Production
# uses Chroma Cloud, so this is dev-only bulk.
**/chroma

# promptfoo eval artifacts - dev tooling, never runs in the deployed image.
**/.promptfoo
chatbot-backend/src/_eval/output

# The other two services in the monorepo. Neither Dockerfile references them,
# and site/ in particular drags in a very large .next build.
cms
site
